 or Vultr's free DDoS protection tiers before purchasing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does ServerHub compare to RackNerd or Vultr?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"ServerHub's $5/mo Pure SSD Starter matches Vultr's $5/mo Cloud Compute entry on sticker price but ships with 2 vCPU + 1 GB RAM + 50 GB SSD vs Vultr's 1 vCPU + 1 GB + 25 GB. ServerHub's 9-DC footprint is mid-size vs Vultr's 32+ regions but offers 10G-port connectivity on every VPS plan. RackNerd's $1.99/mo budget unmanaged tier is cheaper at the floor; ServerHub targets buyers who want a 23-year track record, 10G-ready network, and RAID-10 storage as standard rather than absolute lowest sticker price."}}]}
